###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Hyperparameters and training details are in Appendix G, which was not read; only the variant is encoded as a setting. Cutoffs, embedding sizes, optimizer and learning rate are missing.
# - The four GemNet variants are settings of one registry method (METHODS.md rule 3). The direct-force variants (-dQ, -dT) do not give a conservative force field; a query that needs that distinction must filter on the variant setting.
# - MD17 has two benzene rows in Table 3, from the 2017 and the 2018 data of Chmiela et al.; they are two material/data-set nodes.
# - The reference levels of COLL, MD17 and OC20 are not restated; only MD17@CCSD carries a (generic wave-function) reference calculation, because the paper says 'CCSD or CCSD(T)' without assigning them.
# - OC20 IS2RS and IS2RE results, force cosine, AFbT and ADwT of Table 4 are not encoded.
# - This is a preprint (arXiv v10); the manifest notes 'preprint only', and the DOI is the arXiv DOI (authors from DataCite, without ORCIDs).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
